IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fwa2-common`

-- Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) -- baseline-2026-11: unfair dismissal remedies, orders to stop bullying, and sexual
-- harassment in connection with work.
--
-- SEAT: the dismissed employee ("What can the FWC order for me, and how much compensation at most?"), the worker who
-- is bullied ("Have I been bullied at work? Can I get an order to stop it?") and the person sexually harassed in
-- connection with work ("Is it unlawful? Is the business liable too? By when must I apply, and when can I go to
-- court?").
--
-- PROVISIONS. Part 3-2 Division 4: ss 390, 391(1)-(4), 392(3)-(6) with reg 3.06 (baseline-2026-10 already has who is
-- protected, ss 382-389, the 21 days of s 394, and the half-threshold limb of s 392(5)). Part 6-4B: ss 789FC, 789FD,
-- 789FE(1), 789FF. Part 3-5A: ss 527D, 527E(1), (2), 527F, 527G, 527J(1), (2), 527S(1)(e), 527T. Out: the FWC's
-- procedure (ss 527R(2), 527S(2)-(3), 789FE(2), 527J(4) dismissals for defence and security), ss 527M-527Q, 527CA,
-- 789FH, 527L (WHS law interaction), application fees (s 527H, s 789FC(3), (4)), the defence member rules beyond
-- s 527F(3).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 73 (register id C2026C00355), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2009A00028.txt;
-- Fair Work Regulations 2009, Compilation No. 57 (register id F2026C00996), reg 3.06, as deposited at
-- ../../../fair-work-regulations-2009/registers/source-bundle/F2009L02356.txt. BASELINE; see NOTES.md.

§ `Fair Work Act 2009 -- orders the FWC can make for me`

§§ `ss 390-392 -- unfair dismissal: reinstatement or compensation` -- situation: only if you were dismissed

-- s 390(1): the FWC "may order a person's reinstatement, or the payment of compensation to a person, if: (a) the FWC is
-- satisfied that the person was protected from unfair dismissal ... at the time of being dismissed; and (b) the person
-- has been unfairly dismissed". (2): "only if the person has made an application under section 394". (3): the FWC "must
-- not order the payment of compensation to the person unless: (a) the FWC is satisfied that reinstatement of the person
-- is inappropriate; and (b) the FWC considers an order for payment of compensation is appropriate". Each is the FWC's
-- finding: INPUTS, answered conditionally.
@export Can the FWC order my reinstatement for unfair dismissal (s 390(1), (2))?
GIVEN `I was protected from unfair dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were protected from unfair dismissal when dismissed (minimum employment period served; covered by an award or agreement or under the high income threshold)
      `the FWC finds I was unfairly dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the FWC finds the dismissal harsh, unjust or unreasonable (and not a genuine redundancy or consistent with the Small Business Fair Dismissal Code)
      `I applied under s 394` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied to the FWC for an unfair dismissal remedy (within 21 days, or a further period it allowed)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the FWC order my reinstatement` IF
        `I was protected from unfair dismissal`
    AND `the FWC finds I was unfairly dismissed`
    AND `I applied under s 394`

@export Can the FWC order my employer to pay me compensation instead of reinstating me (s 390(3))?
GIVEN `I was protected from unfair dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were protected from unfair dismissal when dismissed
      `the FWC finds I was unfairly dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the FWC finds the dismissal harsh, unjust or unreasonable
      `I applied under s 394` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied to the FWC for an unfair dismissal remedy
      `the FWC is satisfied reinstatement is inappropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the FWC is satisfied that reinstating you is inappropriate (for example, trust has broken down)
      `the FWC considers compensation appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the FWC considers an order for compensation appropriate in all the circumstances
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the FWC order compensation instead of reinstatement` IF
        `Can the FWC order my reinstatement` `I was protected from unfair dismissal` `the FWC finds I was unfairly dismissed` `I applied under s 394`
    AND `the FWC is satisfied reinstatement is inappropriate`
    AND `the FWC considers compensation appropriate`

-- s 391(1): the order is that "the person's employer at the time of the dismissal reinstate the person" (to the same
-- position, or another "on terms and conditions no less favourable"). s 391(1A): if "(a) the position ... is no longer a
-- position with the person's employer at the time of the dismissal; and (b) that position, or an equivalent position, is
-- a position with an associated entity of the employer", the order "may be an order to the associated entity".
DECLARE `Who can be ordered to reinstate me` IS ONE OF
    `only my employer at the time of the dismissal`
    `my employer, or the associated entity that now has my position`

@export Who can the FWC order to reinstate me (s 391(1), (1A))?
GIVEN `my position is no longer with my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the position you held before the dismissal is no longer a position with your employer
      `an associated entity has my position or an equivalent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that position, or an equivalent one, is now a position with an associated entity of your employer (for example, a related company)
GIVETH A `Who can be ordered to reinstate me`
`Who can be ordered to reinstate me` MEANS
    IF `my position is no longer with my employer` AND `an associated entity has my position or an equivalent`
    THEN `my employer, or the associated entity that now has my position`
    ELSE `only my employer at the time of the dismissal`

-- s 391(2): "If the FWC makes an order under subsection (1) and considers it appropriate to do so, the FWC may also make
-- any order that the FWC considers appropriate to maintain ... (a) the continuity of the person's employment; (b) the
-- period of the person's continuous service". s 391(3): likewise "to cause the employer to pay to the person an amount
-- for the remuneration lost, or likely to have been lost, by the person because of the dismissal". s 391(4): in
-- fixing that amount the FWC "must take into account" (a) remuneration earned from other work between the dismissal
-- and the reinstatement order and (b) remuneration "reasonably likely to be so earned" until the actual reinstatement.
-- Whether an order is appropriate, and the figure, are the FWC's: INPUTS. s 391(4) says "take into account", not
-- "deduct", and sets no cap, so no amount is computed here.
@export With my reinstatement, can the FWC also order my employer to pay me the pay I lost because of the dismissal (s 391(3))?
GIVEN `the FWC orders my reinstatement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the FWC makes a reinstatement order under s 391(1)
      `the FWC considers a lost pay order appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the FWC considers it appropriate also to order payment for the pay you lost, or were likely to lose, because of the dismissal (taking into account what you earned, or are likely to earn, from other work until you are reinstated)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the FWC order my lost pay with reinstatement` IF
        `the FWC orders my reinstatement`
    AND `the FWC considers a lost pay order appropriate`

@export With my reinstatement, can the FWC also order that my employment and my continuous service are unbroken (s 391(2))?
GIVEN `the FWC orders my reinstatement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the FWC makes a reinstatement order under s 391(1)
      `the FWC considers a continuity order appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the FWC considers it appropriate also to order that the continuity of your employment, and your period of continuous service with the employer (or the associated entity), be maintained
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the FWC keep my service continuous with reinstatement` IF
        `the FWC orders my reinstatement`
    AND `the FWC considers a continuity order appropriate`

-- s 392(5): compensation "must not exceed the lesser of: (a) the amount worked out under subsection (6); and (b) half
-- the amount of the high income threshold immediately before the dismissal."
-- s 392(6): "(a) the total amount of remuneration: (i) received by the person; or (ii) to which the person was
-- entitled; (whichever is higher) for any period of employment with the employer during the 26 weeks immediately before
-- the dismissal; and (b) if the employee was on leave without pay or without full pay while so employed during any part
-- of that period--the amount of remuneration taken to have been received by the employee for the period of leave in
-- accordance with the regulations." reg 3.06: the employee "is taken to have received the remuneration that the
-- employee would ordinarily have received during the period of leave".
-- FORK (NOTES.md finding 1): the part pay received during leave "without full pay" could be counted in (a) and again,
-- inside the ordinary remuneration, in (b). This encoding asks for (a) outside the leave and for (b) the ordinary
-- remuneration for the leave, so nothing is counted twice; the other reading adds the part pay again.
-- The high income threshold is set each year under reg 2.13 (encoded in baseline-2026-10 with its floor); here it is an
-- INPUT.
@export What is the most unfair dismissal compensation the FWC can order for me (s 392(5), (6), reg 3.06)?
GIVEN `pay I received in the 26 weeks, outside any unpaid leave` IS A NUMBER @desc The remuneration you received from the employer for the 26 weeks before the dismissal, leaving out any period of leave without pay or without full pay, in dollars
      `pay I was entitled to in the 26 weeks, outside any unpaid leave` IS A NUMBER @desc The remuneration you were entitled to for the same weeks (if different, for example because you were underpaid), in dollars
      `my ordinary pay for any unpaid or part-paid leave in the 26 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc What you would ordinarily have been paid for any period in those 26 weeks when you were on leave without pay or without full pay, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the high income threshold before my dismissal` IS A NUMBER @desc The high income threshold immediately before the dismissal, in dollars a year
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most unfair dismissal compensation` MEANS
    `the smaller of` `the 26 weeks amount` (`the high income threshold before my dismissal` DIVIDED BY 2)
    WHERE
        `the 26 weeks amount` MEANS
            (`the larger of` `pay I received in the 26 weeks, outside any unpaid leave` `pay I was entitled to in the 26 weeks, outside any unpaid leave`)
                PLUS `my ordinary pay for any unpaid or part-paid leave in the 26 weeks`

-- s 392(3): "If the FWC is satisfied that misconduct of a person contributed to the employer's decision to dismiss the
-- person, the FWC must reduce the amount it would otherwise order ... by an appropriate amount". s 392(4): the amount
-- "must not include a component by way of compensation for shock, distress or humiliation". s 392(2): the FWC weighs the
-- employer's viability, length of service, lost remuneration, mitigation, other earnings and anything else relevant --
-- the figure it reaches, and the misconduct reduction, are the FWC's: INPUTS. READING: the cap in s 392(5) applies to
-- the amount after the s 392(3) reduction, since (5) limits "the amount ordered".
@export How much unfair dismissal compensation would I get, after any misconduct reduction and the cap (s 392(3)-(6))?
GIVEN `the amount the FWC assesses` IS A NUMBER @desc The compensation the FWC assesses under s 392(2), before any misconduct reduction and leaving out anything for shock, distress or humiliation, in dollars
      `the misconduct reduction` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the FWC deducts because your misconduct contributed to the decision to dismiss you, in dollars (0 if none)
      `pay I received in the 26 weeks, outside any unpaid leave` IS A NUMBER @desc The remuneration you received for the 26 weeks before the dismissal, leaving out leave without pay or without full pay, in dollars
      `pay I was entitled to in the 26 weeks, outside any unpaid leave` IS A NUMBER @desc The remuneration you were entitled to for the same weeks, in dollars
      `my ordinary pay for any unpaid or part-paid leave in the 26 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc What you would ordinarily have been paid for leave without pay or without full pay in those weeks, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the high income threshold before my dismissal` IS A NUMBER @desc The high income threshold immediately before the dismissal, in dollars a year
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much unfair dismissal compensation would I get` MEANS
    `the smaller of`
        (`the larger of` 0 (`the amount the FWC assesses` MINUS `the misconduct reduction`))
        (`What is the most unfair dismissal compensation` `pay I received in the 26 weeks, outside any unpaid leave` `pay I was entitled to in the 26 weeks, outside any unpaid leave` `my ordinary pay for any unpaid or part-paid leave in the 26 weeks` `the high income threshold before my dismissal`)

§ `Fair Work Act 2009 -- bullied at work (Part 6-4B)` -- situation: only if you have been bullied at work

-- s 789FD(3): a business or undertaking (WHS Act meaning) is "constitutionally-covered" if the person conducting it is
-- "(i) a constitutional corporation; or (ii) the Commonwealth; or (iii) a Commonwealth authority; or (iv) a body
-- corporate incorporated in a Territory", or the business "is conducted principally in a Territory or Commonwealth
-- place". Whether a company is a constitutional corporation (a trading or financial corporation) is an INPUT.
DECLARE `Who runs the business` IS ONE OF
    `a trading or financial company`
    `the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth authority`
    `a company incorporated in a Territory`
    `a State government, sole trader, partnership or other`

@export Is the business where I work a constitutionally-covered business (s 789FD(3))?
GIVEN `who runs the business` IS A `Who runs the business` @desc Who conducts the business or undertaking: a trading or financial company (a constitutional corporation); the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth authority; a company incorporated in a Territory; or a State government, sole trader, partnership or other
      `it is run mainly in a Territory or Commonwealth place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business or undertaking is conducted principally in a Territory (such as the ACT or NT) or a Commonwealth place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a constitutionally-covered business` IF
        `the runner is covered`
    OR  `it is run mainly in a Territory or Commonwealth place`
    WHERE
        `the runner is covered` MEANS
            CONSIDER `who runs the business`
            WHEN `a State government, sole trader, partnership or other` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 789FD(1): "A worker is bullied at work if: (a) while the worker is at work in a constitutionally-covered business:
-- (i) an individual; or (ii) a group of individuals; repeatedly behaves unreasonably towards the worker, or a group of
-- workers of which the worker is a member; and (b) that behaviour creates a risk to health and safety." (2): it "does
-- not apply to reasonable management action carried out in a reasonable manner."
@export Have I been bullied at work in the sense the Fair Work Act uses (s 789FD)?
GIVEN `it happened while I was at work in a constitutionally-covered business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it happened while you were at work in a constitutionally-covered business (ask the s 789FD(3) question first)
      `someone repeatedly behaved unreasonably towards me or my group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an individual or a group of individuals repeatedly behaved unreasonably towards you, or towards a group of workers you belong to
      `the behaviour creates a risk to health and safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that behaviour creates a risk to health and safety
      `it was reasonable management action carried out reasonably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the behaviour was reasonable management action (for example, a fair performance review) carried out in a reasonable manner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I been bullied at work` IF
        `it happened while I was at work in a constitutionally-covered business`
    AND `someone repeatedly behaved unreasonably towards me or my group`
    AND `the behaviour creates a risk to health and safety`
    AND (NOT `it was reasonable management action carried out reasonably`)

-- s 789FC(1): "A worker who reasonably believes that he or she has been bullied at work may apply to the FWC for an
-- order under section 789FF." (2): "worker has the same meaning as in the Work Health and Safety Act 2011, but does not
-- include a member of the Defence Force" -- the WHS meaning (employee, contractor, subcontractor, outworker, apprentice,
-- trainee, student on work experience, volunteer) is an INPUT.
@export Can I apply to the FWC for an order to stop bullying (s 789FC)?
GIVEN `I am a worker in the WHS sense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you do work in any capacity for a business or undertaking: employee, contractor, subcontractor, outworker, apprentice, trainee, student on work experience or volunteer
      `I am a member of the Defence Force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member of the Australian Defence Force
      `I reasonably believe I have been bullied at work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you reasonably believe you have been bullied at work
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I apply for a stop bullying order` IF
        `I am a worker in the WHS sense`
    AND (NOT `I am a member of the Defence Force`)
    AND `I reasonably believe I have been bullied at work`

-- s 789FE(1): "The FWC must start to deal with an application under section 789FC within 14 days after the application
-- is made." (A duty on the FWC; for the worker it is the day by which the application must be taken up.)
@export By when must the FWC start dealing with my application to stop bullying (s 789FE(1))?
GIVEN `I applied on` IS A DATE @desc The day you made the application
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the FWC start on my bullying application` MEANS
    `the day that is` `I applied on` 14

-- s 789FF(1): if a worker has applied and "the FWC is satisfied that: (i) the worker has been bullied at work by an
-- individual or a group of individuals; and (ii) there is a risk that the worker will continue to be bullied at work by
-- the individual or group; then the FWC may make any order it considers appropriate (other than an order requiring
-- payment of a pecuniary amount)". The order can stop the bullying; it cannot award money (see NOTES.md).
@export Can the FWC make an order to stop the bullying (s 789FF)?
GIVEN `I applied under s 789FC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied to the FWC for an order to stop bullying
      `the FWC is satisfied I was bullied at work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the FWC is satisfied you have been bullied at work by an individual or group
      `the FWC is satisfied there is a risk it will continue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the FWC is satisfied there is a risk you will continue to be bullied at work by that individual or group (for example, you still work with them)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the FWC order the bullying to stop` IF
        `I applied under s 789FC`
    AND `the FWC is satisfied I was bullied at work`
    AND `the FWC is satisfied there is a risk it will continue`

§ `Fair Work Act 2009 -- sexual harassment in connection with work (Part 3-5A)` -- situation: only if you have been sexually harassed

-- s 527D(1): "A person (the first person) must not sexually harass another person (the second person) who is: (a) a
-- worker in a business or undertaking; or (b) seeking to become a worker in a particular business or undertaking; or
-- (c) a person conducting a business or undertaking; if the harassment occurs in connection with the second person
-- being a person of the kind mentioned". s 12: "sexually harass has the meaning given by section 28A of the Sex
-- Discrimination Act 1984" -- borrowed, so an INPUT. s 527D(2): worker has its WHS Act meaning.
DECLARE `My role` IS ONE OF
    `a worker in a business or undertaking`
    `seeking to become a worker in a particular business`
    `a person conducting a business or undertaking`
    `none of these`

@export Was I sexually harassed in breach of the Fair Work Act (s 527D)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A `My role` @desc Your role: a worker in a business or undertaking (employee, contractor, volunteer, trainee and the like); seeking to become a worker in a particular business; a person conducting a business or undertaking; or none of these
      `I was sexually harassed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were sexually harassed (unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature, a reasonable person would anticipate you would be offended, humiliated or intimidated: Sex Discrimination Act s 28A)
      `it was in connection with that role` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the harassment happened in connection with your being in that role (at work, at a work event, by a colleague or client, and the like)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I sexually harassed in breach of s 527D` IF
        `I have a protected role`
    AND `I was sexually harassed`
    AND `it was in connection with that role`
    WHERE
        `I have a protected role` MEANS
            CONSIDER `my role`
            WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 527E(1): if an employee or agent of a person (the principal) does, "in connection with the employment of the
-- employee or with the duties of the agent as an agent, an act that contravenes subsection 527D(1)", the Act applies "as
-- if the principal had also done the act". (2): not "if the principal proves that the principal took all reasonable
-- steps to prevent the employee or agent from doing acts that would contravene subsection 527D(1)."
@export Is the harasser's employer (or principal) liable too (s 527E)?
GIVEN `the harassment broke s 527D` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the harassment was in breach of s 527D (ask that question first)
      `the harasser is an employee or agent of the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the harasser is an employee or agent of a business or person (the principal)
      `it was in connection with their employment or agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they did it in connection with their employment, or their duties as an agent
      `the principal proves it took all reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the principal proves it took all reasonable steps to prevent its employees or agents from sexually harassing (training, policies, acting on complaints)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the harasser's employer liable too` IF
        `the harassment broke s 527D`
    AND `the harasser is an employee or agent of the business`
    AND `it was in connection with their employment or agency`
    AND (NOT `the principal proves it took all reasonable steps to prevent it`)

-- s 527F(1), (2): the aggrieved person (or an industrial association entitled to represent them) "may apply for the FWC
-- to do either or both of the following ...: (a) make an order (a stop sexual harassment order) ...; (b) otherwise deal
-- with the dispute." (3): "Despite paragraph (1)(a), a person ... cannot, except as provided by the regulations, apply
-- for the FWC to make a stop sexual harassment order ... if the aggrieved person was a defence member ... at the time
-- the sexual harassment allegedly occurred." No such regulation is encoded: a defence member's answer is NOTHING.
@export Can I ask the FWC for a stop sexual harassment order (s 527F)?
GIVEN `I allege I was sexually harassed in breach of Division 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say you were sexually harassed in connection with work (s 527D)
      `I was a defence member when it happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a member of the Defence Force when the harassment allegedly happened
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I ask for a stop sexual harassment order` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I allege I was sexually harassed in breach of Division 2`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `I was a defence member when it happened`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 527G: "The FWC may dismiss an application that is made under section 527F more than 24 months after the
-- contravention, or the last of the contraventions, of Division 2 is alleged to have occurred."
@export By when should I apply to the FWC about sexual harassment so that it cannot be dismissed as late (s 527G)?
GIVEN `the last harassment happened on` IS A DATE @desc The day of the harassment (or of the last incident, if more than one)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when should I apply about sexual harassment` MEANS
    `the day some months after` `the last harassment happened on` 24

@export Can the FWC dismiss my sexual harassment application because it is more than 24 months late (s 527G)?
GIVEN `the last harassment happened on` IS A DATE @desc The day of the harassment (or of the last incident, if more than one)
      `I apply on` IS A DATE @desc The day you lodge (or lodged) the application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my sexual harassment application be dismissed as late` IF
    NOT (`falls on or before` `I apply on` (`By when should I apply about sexual harassment` `the last harassment happened on`))

-- s 527J(1): if the application includes one for a stop sexual harassment order and "the FWC is satisfied that: (i) the
-- aggrieved person has been sexually harassed in contravention of Division 2 by one or more persons; and (ii) there is a
-- risk that the aggrieved person will continue to be sexually harassed ... by the person or persons; then the FWC may
-- make any order it considers appropriate (other than an order requiring payment of a pecuniary amount)". (2): the FWC
-- "must start to deal with the application ... within 14 days after the application is made."
@export Can the FWC make an order to stop the sexual harassment (s 527J(1))?
GIVEN `I asked for a stop sexual harassment order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your s 527F application includes an application for a stop sexual harassment order
      `the FWC is satisfied I was sexually harassed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the FWC is satisfied you were sexually harassed in breach of s 527D by one or more persons
      `the FWC is satisfied there is a risk it will continue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the FWC is satisfied there is a risk you will continue to be sexually harassed by them
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the FWC order the sexual harassment to stop` IF
        `I asked for a stop sexual harassment order`
    AND `the FWC is satisfied I was sexually harassed`
    AND `the FWC is satisfied there is a risk it will continue`

@export By when must the FWC start dealing with my application for a stop sexual harassment order (s 527J(2))?
GIVEN `I applied on` IS A DATE @desc The day you made the application
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the FWC start on my stop sexual harassment application` MEANS
    `the day that is` `I applied on` 14

-- s 527S(1): the FWC may arbitrate after a s 527R(3)(a) certificate if parties including at least one aggrieved person
-- and one respondent jointly notify it, the notice "given to the FWC within 60 days after the day the certificate is
-- issued, or within such period as the FWC allows".
@export By when must we tell the FWC that we agree to arbitration of my sexual harassment dispute (s 527S(1)(e))?
GIVEN `the certificate was issued on` IS A DATE @desc The day the FWC issued its certificate that attempts to resolve the dispute have failed
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must we agree to arbitration of my sexual harassment dispute` MEANS
    `the day that is` `the certificate was issued on` 60

-- s 527T(1): no "sexual harassment court application" unless "(a) ... (i) the FWC has issued a certificate under
-- paragraph 527R(3)(a) ...; (ii) the ... application is made within a period specified in subsection (3); or (b) the ...
-- application includes an application for an interim injunction." (3): "(a) 60 days after the day the certificate is
-- issued; (b) if the person is removed under paragraph 527S(2)(a) as a party to the dispute--14 days after the person is
-- given notice ... of the removal; (c) such period as the court allows". READING (NOTES.md finding 2): a removed party
-- may use whichever of (a) and (b) ends later, since each is "a period specified".
@export By when must I start a sexual harassment case in court after the FWC's certificate (s 527T(3))?
GIVEN `the certificate was issued on` IS A DATE @desc The day the FWC issued its certificate that attempts to resolve the dispute have failed
      `I was removed as a party when others agreed to arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the FWC removed you as a party because other parties agreed to arbitration without you
      `I was given notice of my removal on` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given notice of the removal (any date if you were not removed)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I go to court about sexual harassment` MEANS
    IF `I was removed as a party when others agreed to arbitration`
       AND Day (`the day that is` `I was given notice of my removal on` 14) GREATER THAN Day (`the day that is` `the certificate was issued on` 60)
    THEN `the day that is` `I was given notice of my removal on` 14
    ELSE `the day that is` `the certificate was issued on` 60

-- s 527T note: once parties agree to arbitration, s 734A "generally" bars a court application between them; s 734A is
-- not encoded, so where I agreed to arbitration the answer is NOTHING.
@export Can I take my sexual harassment dispute to court (s 527T)?
GIVEN `the FWC issued a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the FWC has issued its certificate that attempts to resolve the dispute have failed
      `the certificate was issued on` IS A DATE @desc The day the certificate was issued (any date if there is none)
      `I was removed as a party when others agreed to arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the FWC removed you as a party because other parties agreed to arbitration without you
      `I was given notice of my removal on` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given notice of the removal (any date if you were not removed)
      `I file in court on` IS A DATE @desc The day you file (or filed) the court application
      `the court allows a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are late, whether the court allows a longer period
      `my application includes an interim injunction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your court application includes an application for an interim injunction
      `I agreed to FWC arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you joined in notifying the FWC that you agree to it arbitrating the dispute
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I take my sexual harassment dispute to court` MEANS
    IF `I agreed to FWC arbitration`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (   (    `the FWC issued a certificate`
                   AND (   `falls on or before` `I file in court on` (`By when must I go to court about sexual harassment` `the certificate was issued on` `I was removed as a party when others agreed to arbitration` `I was given notice of my removal on`)
                        OR `the court allows a longer period`))
               OR `my application includes an interim injunction`)
